{"chunk_id":"R2-1900560-005","collection":"ran2_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Ericsson"],"tdocNumber":"R2-1900560","title":"Msg3 Quality Report Format eMTC"},"point_id":"334135215814418722"}
As it is clear from Sections 2.1 and 2.2, regardless on the solution adopted, it is required to extend the minimum TBS for Msg3. As it was already mentioned there are no enough spare bits in legacy messages to implement the new indication. The legacy RRC messages have been dimensioned to generate a MAC PDU fitting exactly a TBS size of 72 bits for RRCConnectionResumeRequest with full resumeID and 56 bits for all the other ones. In principle the messages may be extended only by the few necessary bits, but the next smallest TBS sizes available according to Table 3 and Table 4 (adopted from TS36.213), with respect to the legacy RRC messages, are 88 and 72 bits, which are 16 bits larger than the aforementioned legacy sizes. An RRC message extended by less than 16 bits would lead to a MAC PDU with padding bits which cannot be used. Implementing a 16 bits extension of the RRC messages allows us to have more spare bits available for future non-critical extensions compared to MAC CE solution. Table 3: TBS table for Msg3 in CE mode A Table 4: TBS table for Msg3 in CE mode B In the same way the total size required to carry the MAC CE is 16 bits. The extensions proposed in Section 2.1 and 2.2 are compliant to the above discussion. Both MAC CE and RRC extension-based solutions require an extension of the minimum TBS of at least 16 bits.

{"chunk_id":"R2-2100816-002","collection":"ran2_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Sharp"],"tdocNumber":"R2-2100816","title":"TRS/CSI-RS for idle and inactive mode UE"},"point_id":"17649460165330909900"}
This paper discussed the configuration of TRS/CSI-RS occasion for idle/inactive mode, based on the discussion following proposals are provided: Proposal 1: Other SI (i.e. not MIB or SIB1) is used for the configuration of TRS/CSI occasions for idle/inactive mode. Proposal 2: RAN2 to discuss whether to extend the existing SIB or introduce new SIB when RAN1 achieved more detailed conclusions on the TRS/CSI-RS configuration. Proposal 3: RRC release message can be used if dedicated TRS/CSI-RS configuration for idle/inactive mode is allowed. Proposal 4: RAN2 to wait more RAN1 input before starting to discuss potential signalling design of availability of the TRS/CSI-RS configuration. R1-2009848, LS on signalling method for TRS/CSI-RS occasion(s) for idle/inactive UE(s), RAN1#103-e. RAN1#103-e meeting report.

{"chunk_id":"R2-2600652-002","collection":"ran2_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Ericsson"],"tdocNumber":"R2-2600652","title":"Main principles for Dynamic L1 measurement and reporting configuration change"},"point_id":"15723391684355591238"}
 in the previous sections we propose the following: Proposal 1 The targeted configurations for dynamic activation and deactivation are LTM-CSI-ReportConfig and LTM-CSI-ResourceConfig. Proposal 2 Only the activation/deactivation status is dynamically changed, i.e. no content within the report or resource configuration structure can be changed dynamically by the new MAC CE. Proposal 3 Activating a report configuration also implicitly activates the related resource configuration(s). Proposal 4 The existing RRC configuration for LTM-CSI-ReportConfig and LTM-CSI-ResourceConfig is reused and updated with an activation status flag. Proposal 5 If the RRC configuration for LTM-CSI-ReportConfig does not contain an activation status flag the configuration is considered activated (as in legacy). Proposal 6 Introduce new MAC CE(s) to activate/deactivate report/resource configuration(s), details are for further studies.
